{
  "info": {
    "name": "COIT20273 \u2014 AI-Powered Study Notes Generator API",
    "description": "Shared API collection for the capstone project.\n\n**Owner of folders 1-4:** Member 3 (Natthapong Rinsakul) \u2014 Document Processing and AI Integration subsystems.\n**Folder 0** contains Member 2's authentication endpoints, included because a JWT is required to call anything else.\n\n## Setup\n1. Start the backend: `cd backend && PORT=5099 node src/server.js`\n2. Check the `baseUrl` collection variable matches your port.\n3. Run **0. Setup \u2192 Register**, then **Login**. The token is captured automatically into the `token` variable \u2014 no copying required.\n4. Run **1. Upload** with a file selected. `fileId` is captured automatically.\n5. Run **2. Consent \u2192 Grant consent** before any AI request (FR17.1).\n\n## Security note\nDo not commit a Postman *environment* containing a real JWT or GEMINI_API_KEY. Keep secrets in `backend/.env`, which is git-ignored.\n\nEndpoint contracts are documented in `docs/api-spec.md`.\n\n## Postman settings for the Collection Runner\nFound during the first full run on 3 September 2026:\n\n- **Select a file, not a folder**, for the upload request, or Postman reports `EISDIR: illegal operation on a directory`.\n- Enable **Settings \u2192 General \u2192 Read files outside working directory**, or the upload returns 400 because Postman detaches the local file path.\n- Uncheck **Stop run if an error occurs** in the Runner, since folder 5 deliberately produces error responses.\n- Consent state is handled automatically: folder 2 restores it, and folder 5's CONSENT_REQUIRED request revokes and restores it around itself. No request needs to be unchecked.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5099",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "fileId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "outputId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "quizOutputId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "quizAnswers",
      "value": "[]",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "quizAnswersPartial",
      "value": "[]",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup \u2014 authentication (Member 2's endpoints)",
      "description": "Owned by Member 2. Included so the collection is usable end to end: every other request needs a JWT.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Confirms the server is running. No authentication required."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Register",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/register",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users",
                "register"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates an account (FR1). Change the e-mail if it already exists.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"full_name\": \"Postman Test User\",\n  \"email\": \"postman-test@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// 201 on success, 400 if the e-mail is already registered",
                  "pm.test('registered or already exists', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect([201, 400]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (captures token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/users/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "users",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns a JWT (FR2). A test script saves it into the `token` collection variable, so later requests authenticate automatically.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"postman-test@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Passw0rd!\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (body.token) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.token);",
                  "  console.log('Token saved to collection variable.');",
                  "} else {",
                  "  console.warn('No token in response \u2014 check the credentials.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Profile (verifies the token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/profile",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "profile"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the decoded user from the JWT. Use this to confirm the token works."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Upload, extraction and document list (FR6, FR8)",
      "description": "Upload validation and text extraction (Member 3), plus the uploaded-files list endpoint owned by Member 1.\n\nValidation is by file **extension**, not MIME type, because MIME type is client-supplied and inconsistent.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Upload document (captures fileId)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/upload",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "upload"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Uploads a .pdf, .docx or .txt file, extracts its text and stores both.\n\n**Before sending:** open the Body tab and select a file for the `file` key \u2014 Postman cannot store the file path in a shared collection.\n\nMax 15 MB (FR6.2). The response includes `file_id`, which the test script captures into the `fileId` variable for the AI requests that follow.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Select a .pdf, .docx or .txt file (max 15 MB)"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('text was extracted', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(b.text_length).to.be.above(0));",
                  "console.log('Extracted characters:', b.text_length);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('fileId', b.file.file_id);",
                  "console.log('fileId saved:', b.file.file_id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List my uploaded documents (Member 1's endpoint)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/uploaded",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "uploaded"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Owned by Member 1 (added 20 Aug 2026, commit c7d49df). Returns every document belonging to the authenticated user, newest first, without the extracted text.\n\nIncluded here so the collection covers the full document workflow. The `file_id` values returned can be passed directly to POST /api/ai/generate."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('files is an array', () => pm.expect(b.files).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "console.log('Documents found:', b.files.length);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get uploaded document",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/uploaded/{{fileId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "uploaded",
                "{{fileId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the stored document and its extracted text. Scoped to the authenticated user \u2014 another user's file returns 404 (NFR3)."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. AI consent (FR17, NFR11) \u2014 Member 3",
      "description": "Consent is recorded as an append-only audit trail: each decision is a new row and current consent is the most recent one. Consent is required before any content is sent to Gemini, and is re-checked on every generation request.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Grant consent",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/consent",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "consent"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Records consent (FR17.1). Required before any AI generation succeeds.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"granted\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get consent status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/consent",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "consent"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the most recent decision. `consent: null` means the user has never decided \u2014 that is not an error, show the consent prompt."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Revoke consent",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/consent",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "consent"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Revokes consent (FR17.2). The next request restores it so folder 3 can run \u2014 the refusal behaviour itself is proved in folder 5, which manages its own state.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"revoked\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Grant consent again (restore state)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/consent",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "consent"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Re-grants consent so the collection leaves this folder in a state the AI requests in folder 3 can use. Without this the run order would revoke consent and every generation request would return 403.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"status\": \"granted\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('consent is granted again', () =>",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().consent.status).to.eql('granted'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. AI generation (FR9-FR12, FR16) \u2014 Member 3",
      "description": "Four output types. **Consent is enforced server-side**, not by the interface.\n\n`content` is a **string** for summary and explanation, and an **array** for flashcards and quiz \u2014 switch on `output_type` before reading it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Generate summary (FR9)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ai/generate",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ai",
                "generate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Prose summary of the document's key concepts and definitions.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"file_id\": \"{{fileId}}\",\n  \"output_type\": \"summary\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('carries the AI-generated label (FR16.1)', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(b.output.is_ai_generated).to.be.true;",
                  "  pm.expect(b.disclaimer).to.be.a('string');",
