    {
      "name": "4. Quiz attempts and scoring (FR11.2) \u2014 Member 3",
      "description": "Marking happens on the server against the stored quiz, so the client cannot influence its own score. Each attempt is a new row, so retakes are preserved for the progress dashboard (FR14).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Submit quiz attempt",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/ai/quiz/{{quizOutputId}}/attempt",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "ai",
                "quiz",
                "{{quizOutputId}}",
                "attempt"
              ]
            },
            "description": "One answer per question, in order. Use `null` for unanswered questions - partial attempts are recorded and score zero for those.\n\n`{{quizAnswers}}` is populated automatically by **Generate quiz**, sized to that quiz's question count, so this request works without editing. Run Generate quiz first.\n\nTo demonstrate partial scoring, swap `{{quizAnswers}}` for `{{quizAnswersPartial}}` - first question answered, the rest left null.",
